pages.content:
Iterating through an array is essential for searching, filtering, aggregating, and transforming elements.

### Standard Indexed For Loop vs Enhanced For-Each Loop

```java
public class ArrayIterationDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[] scores = {85, 92, 78, 90, 88};

        // 1. Standard Indexed Loop (Use when you need the index or reverse order)
        System.out.println("--- Indexed Loop (Reverse) ---");
        for (int i = scores.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            System.out.print(scores[i] + " ");
        }
        System.out.println();

        // 2. Enhanced For-Each Loop (Cleanest when you only need values)
        System.out.println("--- Enhanced For Loop ---");
        int sum = 0;
        for (int score : scores) {
            sum += score;
        }
        double average = (double) sum / scores.length;
        System.out.println("Total: " + sum + ", Average: " + average);
    }
}
```

**Output:**
```default
--- Indexed Loop (Reverse) ---
88 90 78 92 85 
--- Enhanced For Loop ---
Total: 433, Average: 86.6
```

