pages.content:
Elements in an `ArrayList` are accessed by position using the **`.get(int index)`** method.

### Syntax and Bounds Checking

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class ArrayListAccessDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ArrayList<String> fruits = new ArrayList<>();
        fruits.add("Apple");  // index 0
        fruits.add("Banana"); // index 1
        fruits.add("Cherry"); // index 2

        // Retrieve by index
        String first = fruits.get(0);
        String last = fruits.get(fruits.size() - 1);

        System.out.println("First: " + first + ", Last: " + last);
    }
}
```

### IndexOutOfBoundsException
The valid index range for an `ArrayList` is:
$$0 \le \text{index} < \text{list.size()}$$

Calling `list.get(index)` where `index >= list.size()` or `index < 0` immediately throws **`IndexOutOfBoundsException`**:

```java
fruits.get(3); // RUNTIME ERROR: IndexOutOfBoundsException: Index 3 out of bounds for length 3
```

