pages.content:
Traversing an `ArrayList` can be done using multiple approaches depending on whether you need access to index positions or need to safely modify elements during traversal.

### 3 Ways to Iterate an ArrayList

#### 1. Indexed For Loop (Index Available)
```java
for (int i = 0; i < list.size(); i++) {
    System.out.println("Index " + i + ": " + list.get(i));
}
```

#### 2. Enhanced For-Each Loop (Read-Only Sequential)
```java
for (String item : list) {
    System.out.println(item);
}
```

#### 3. Iterator (Safe Modification During Traversal)
```java
Iterator<String> it = list.iterator();
while (it.hasNext()) {
    String item = it.next();
    if (item.startsWith("Temp")) {
        it.remove(); // Safe removal! Does not throw ConcurrentModificationException
    }
}
```

