pages.content:
The `add(int index, E element)` method allows inserting an element at any arbitrary position within an `ArrayList`.

### Insertion Mechanics & Shifting

When an element is inserted at position `index`:
1. All existing elements from `index` up to `size() - 1` are **shifted one position to the right**.
2. The new element is placed into the vacated position at `index`.
3. The list's `size()` increases by 1.

```java
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class InsertIndexDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        ArrayList<String> letters = new ArrayList<>();
        letters.add("A");
        letters.add("C");
        letters.add("D");

        System.out.println("Before insert: " + letters); // [A, C, D]

        // Insert "B" at index 1
        letters.add(1, "B");
        System.out.println("After insert: " + letters);  // [A, B, C, D]

        // Inserting at index equal to size() appends to the end
        letters.add(letters.size(), "E");
        System.out.println("Appended: " + letters);      // [A, B, C, D, E]
    }
}
```

> [!WARNING]
> Valid insertion indices range from `0` to `size()` inclusive. Attempting to insert at `index > size()` or `index < 0` throws `IndexOutOfBoundsException`.

