pages.content:
Iterating through a 2D array requires **nested loops**: an outer loop to iterate over rows, and an inner loop to iterate over columns within each row.

### Safe Traversal Supporting Jagged Arrays

Always use `matrix[i].length` for the inner loop condition to ensure your code works correctly for both rectangular and jagged matrices:

```java
public class MatrixTraversalDemo {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] grid = {
            {10, 20},
            {30, 40, 50},
            {60}
        };

        // Standard Nested For Loop
        for (int i = 0; i < grid.length; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < grid[i].length; j++) {
                System.out.print(grid[i][j] + " ");
            }
            System.out.println();
        }

        // Enhanced For-Each Loop (Cleanest for read-only processing)
        int sum = 0;
        for (int[] row : grid) {
            for (int val : row) {
                sum += val;
            }
        }
        System.out.println("Sum of all elements: " + sum); // 210
    }
}
```

**Output:**
```default
10 20 
30 40 50 
60 
Sum of all elements: 210
```

