pages.content:
Understanding matrix traversal patterns is vital for performance optimization and algorithm implementation.

### Row-Major vs Column-Major Traversal

- **Row-Major Traversal:** Outer loop traverses rows, inner loop traverses columns (`grid[row][col]`). Matches CPU memory layout, maximizing **cache hits**.
- **Column-Major Traversal:** Outer loop traverses columns, inner loop traverses rows (`grid[row][col]`). Useful for column-wise aggregations (e.g. column totals).

```java
public class MatrixOperations {
    // Transpose a square matrix (swap rows and columns)
    public static int[][] transpose(int[][] matrix) {
        int n = matrix.length;
        int[][] result = new int[n][n];

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                result[j][i] = matrix[i][j]; // Swap indices
            }
        }
        return result;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int[][] mat = {
            {1, 2},
            {3, 4}
        };
        int[][] transposed = transpose(mat);
        // Result:
        // {1, 3}
        // {2, 4}
    }
}
```

